Baby Steerling: Interpretable Language Models
Copyright 2026 PyC Team

This project independently implements ideas described in Guide Labs' technical report
"Scaling Inherently Interpretable Language Models" and their public Steerling repository
(https://github.com/guidelabs/steerling, Apache License 2.0):

  - The Steerling concept-bottleneck architecture (babysteerling/nn.py, loss.py, training.py):
    a language model whose hidden state is decomposed into known-concept, unknown-concept, and
    residual contributions, trained with dedicated concept/reconstruction/independence losses.
  - The Atlas concept-dataset construction pipeline (babysteerling/data/atlas/): tagging text
    with an LLM, clustering tags into a canonical concept library, and assigning concepts back
    to a training corpus.

This is an independent, from-scratch implementation written from based on public information, scaled
down to train in minutes on a laptop rather than at their production scale. This project is
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE) in the same spirit as the original.
